# Goldens and curated fixtures are Docker-Linux-authored and LF-canonical (DL-0016).
# Windows checkouts must not re-mangle them to CRLF, and Windows-side git must not
# re-mangle them back on commit either -- force LF for everything under suites/.
suites/**       text eol=lf

# Never re-encode binary-ish artifacts KiCad might one day emit under a golden
# (e.g. a future STEP/3D opt-in suite, DL-0012) even though none exist yet in M0.
suites/**/*.step -text
suites/**/*.stp  -text
suites/**/*.png  -text
suites/**/*.pdf  -text

# Runner source: normal git-native line-ending handling (no forced LF), since
# contributors edit it directly with their own editor's line endings.
